1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Imagine a local shop needs only to know that a customer is over 18.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
But a credential may contain a birth date, document number, and address.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Different schemas can push a simple check toward over-collection.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Sovra starts with a smaller question: age_over_18.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Follow that question through two fictional relying-party apps.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
NovaBank and CornerCellar ask the same eligibility question.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
The holder reviews the exact evidence before choosing to share it.

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Both app flows are local and synthetic.

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The core Compose file starts PostgreSQL, Keycloak, a seed job, and a quarantine worker.

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Two backend instances, app-a and app-b, share the same PostgreSQL database.

11
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:44,000
That is the application replica setup; it is not issuer-level separation.

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
A separate Compose file powers the unfamiliar-schema demonstration with two issuer nodes.

13
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Node A owns its database and signing key. Node B owns a different database and key.

14
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The plan selects the issuer. Public trust metadata is copied; credentials and private keys stay local to each node.

15
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The browser sends a small case selector for Fjord.

16
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,000
The demo server builds a scoped intent and asks the central planner to find a compatible claim.

17
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
The real response proposes candidate-only and returns isAdult on synth-2.

18
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,000
A deterministic guard checks that plan and returns GUARD_ACCEPTED.

19
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,000
The browser never chooses or echoes the unfamiliar field.

20
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Before issuance, the holder sees the purpose, issuer, exact claim, expiry, and plan hash.

21
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,000
They can approve, decline, or go back. No proof is shared before approval.

22
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:44,000
This plan, guard response, and consent screen came from the running synthetic flow.

23
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,000
After approval, the selected issuer signs a scoped synthetic credential.

24
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Verification checks the evidence and records an accepted decision.

25
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,000
The relying party receives one bounded result, not a source identity record.

26
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,000
NovaBank records eligibility evidence in its synthetic onboarding flow.

27
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:07,000
CornerCellar places a fictional demo order after the synthetic age check.

28
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:12,000
These are local browser demos, not external production services.

29
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Now test an incompatible input: employment tenure cannot prove age.

30
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The fixture planner returns NO_PATH with a null plan.

31
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,000
No guard result, credential, or consent request follows.

32
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Credentials use P-256/ES256 signatures; vault objects use AES-GCM encryption.

33
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Each object version gets a fresh 32-byte data key and 12-byte nonce.

34
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,000
AES-GCM binds holder identity as associated data.

35
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,000
HKDF-SHA256 derives versioned tenant wrapping keys in this synthetic software provider.

36
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Production KMS is unavailable; its production gate fails closed.

37
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The browser age-check route never reads vault documents.

38
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Ask, plan, guard, consent, and verify are separate steps.

39
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Synthetic fixtures only. FIXTURE planner, live AI off, one local host.

40
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,000
No legal KYC, zero-knowledge proof, production hosting, or external conformance is shown.
